SUSPECTED BUG: a pointer that is nil on one path and allocated on the other loses both its typed-nil Origin and its Unwrap chain.
`var oe *kverr.OpError; if key == "" { oe = &kverr.OpError{Op: "probe", Err: kverr.ErrEmptyKey} }; return oe`.
Expected 2 entries: sentinel kverr.ErrEmptyKey under *kverr.OpError.Unwrap, and concrete *kverr.OpError [typed nil] for the path that leaves oe nil
(the direct form `var p *T; return p` is reported as typed nil, see e2e origins/typed_nil).
Actual: 1 bare `concrete *kverr.OpError` entry: no [typed nil], and kverr.ErrEmptyKey is dropped without an Unresolved entry, although errors.Is(err, kverr.ErrEmptyKey) holds.
